From 7a5a224cc326d9cc0c50ed99b8f145c32019851c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 07:54:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(vulkan): Q5_K mat-vec activation hoist behind spec
 constant (R48 phase 1)

The weight decode of mul_mat_vec_q5_k.comp was already shared across NUM_COLS
columns upstream; the activation side was not. With the row loop outermost the
eight vec2 loads of data_b were issued num_rows times per superblock per column
for bytes that do not depend on the row. Arm 1 loads each activation vector once
per superblock and reuses it across all rows, so the term that grows with batch
width is divided by NUM_ROWS while the weight term is untouched.

Both arms call the same decode_superblock() and accumulate_column(), so the fma
chains, operand order and accumulation order into temp[j][n] are one piece of
code and the arms are bit-identical by construction. Specialization constant 3
(GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_B_HOIST, default 1) lets one binary serve both arms; the opt-out
is load-bearing because the hoisted arm holds NUM_ROWS rows of decoded weights
live across the column loop, and lane-230 measured that shape spilling on this
device class.

Also adds a device-probed GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_MMVQ_N1 override. Q5_K at n == 1 is the
only width still served by the q8_1 MMVQ shader on AMD; the override sends it to
the f32 shader so the whole 1..8 sweep is one kernel. It defaults to the shipped
route, so no default moves.

Correctness: test-backend-ops -o MUL_MAT -b Vulkan0 -p type_a=q5_K is green in
both arms (61 cases, 0 FAIL, unset and GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_B_HOIST=0). No perf run,
no model run. Q6_K registrations and mul_mat_vec_q6_k.comp are untouched.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-234 R48 Q5_K, Opus 5 MEDIUM kernel-maker)
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED - correctness only; pairing owed to HQ chain134
