+`:7105` / `:7171` are byte-for-byte unchanged — `vulkan-q6k-matvec-direct-scales` cannot regress from
+this diff. Q6_K appears in the new perf block only as a read-only witness.
+
+**No `vulkan-shaders-gen.cpp` change is needed.** No shader file was added or renamed; a new
+`constant_id` requires no registration. Precedent checked: `mul_mat_vec_q6_k.comp:28` declares
+`constant_id = 3` and `vulkan-shaders-gen.cpp` mentions neither it nor any other spec constant.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Why item (c) — 16-byte coalesced loads — was NOT forced
+
+The two `u16` values packed into each `qs` word are **not adjacent**:
+
+```glsl
+uint32_t(data_a_packed16[ib].qs[q_offset / 2]) | (uint32_t(data_a_packed16[ib].qs[q_offset / 2 + 8]) << 16)
+```
+
+Indices `k` and `k + 8` are **16 bytes apart**. A `packed32` view supplies the adjacent pair
+`(2k, 2k+1)`, which is a different set of weights. The gather is deliberate: the two halves feed
+different 4-weight groups that receive different `qh` offsets and different sub-block scales.
+
+So the `packed32` alias **is** available (CHECKED: `types.glsl:446` defines
+`A_TYPE_PACKED32 = block_q5_K_packed32` under `DATA_A_Q5_K`; `mul_mat_vec_iface.glsl:16` binds
+`data_a_packed32` whenever that macro exists), but it **cannot** be substituted without also
+re-deriving the thread→weight mapping. A `block_q5_K_packed128` (`uvec4`) view also exists and is
+unused by this shader. Rewriting the mapping is a genuine change with a genuine payoff — 28 B of
+scattered requests per thread-row become a handful of wide ones — but it is a **from-scratch index
+derivation that I cannot compile or test**, and a wrong mapping here is silent wrong math, not a
+crash. **Named and left for a phase that can run `test-backend-ops`.**
+
+---
+
+## 6. Self-review checklist (performed instead of compiling)
+
+| Check | Result |
+|---|---|
+| **Spec constant id** | `constant_id = 3`. Ids 0/1/2 are `BLOCK_SIZE`/`NUM_ROWS`/`NUM_COLS` (`mul_mat_vec_base.glsl:89-91`). 3 is free in this shader. Q6_K uses 3 for its own constant in its own shader — no conflict, separate modules. |
+| **Positional binding** | `ggml_vk_create_pipeline` maps the constants vector positionally to ids `0..n-1`. `{wg_size_subgroup16, rm_kq, i+1, q5k_b_hoist}` → ids 0,1,2,3. Matches the Q6_K call's shape exactly. |
+| **Bindings / push constants** | Untouched. `mul_mat_vec_num_bindings` (5) and `sizeof(vk_mat_vec_push_constants)` unchanged in both edited calls. No new buffer, no new push-constant field. |
+| **Types** | `dm` is `FLOAT_TYPEV2` (matches `data_a[].dm` cast, as before). `sc`/`q4` are `FLOAT_TYPE`, the type the old locals used. B stays `vec2` from `data_b_v2` (`mul_mat_vec_iface.glsl:21`). `accumulate_column` takes `inout FLOAT_TYPE` and writes `temp[j][n]` — same lvalue as before. |
+| **Spec-constant-sized locals** | `dm[NUM_ROWS]`, `sc[NUM_ROWS][8]`, `q4[NUM_ROWS][16]`. Legal: `temp[NUM_COLS][NUM_ROWS]` and `tmpsh[NUM_COLS][NUM_ROWS][BLOCK_SIZE]` already do this in the same translation unit. |
+| **Tail arm** | `main()` may call `compute_outputs(first_row, p.stride_d - first_row)` with `num_rows < NUM_ROWS`. Loops run `n < num_rows`; arrays are sized `NUM_ROWS >= num_rows`. **In bounds.** New test rows `m = 17407` and `m = 7` exercise it — previously uncovered at these shapes. |
+| **Numerics** | Reordering `j`/`n` does **not** change the order of updates to any single `temp[j][n]` cell: each cell is still updated once per superblock, in increasing `i`. Operands, fma nesting and `-dm.y` sign are byte-copies of the original. **Expected bit-identical**, hence no tolerance change. |
+| **Index arithmetic** | Old `ib0 + i` with `ib0 = a_offset + (first_row+n)*num_blocks_per_row`; new `ib = a_offset + row*num_blocks_per_row + i` with `row = first_row + n`. Algebraically identical. B offsets `b1`/`b2` are the old expressions with the common subexpression named. |
+| **`_id` path** | `mul_mat_vec_q5_k.comp` is also the `_id` shader (under `MUL_MAT_ID`), so the hoist applies there too. `:7246` now passes `{wg_size_subgroup16, rm_kq, 1, q5k_b_hoist}` — the explicit `1` is `NUM_COLS`, needed because the vector binds positionally and a 3-element form would put the hoist on id 2. `NUM_COLS = 1` is the value it already defaulted to, so nothing else moves. `q5k_b_hoist` is in scope at `:7246` (declared in the `for (w)` body, same block, CHECKED by indentation). The constants argument is a `std::vector<uint32_t>` with no fixed arity, so a 4-element form is accepted on the `_id` layout as it is on the dmmv one. |
+| **Shader-gen** | No change required (see §4). |
+| **Default movement (F-08)** | Routing default **unchanged** — unset `GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_MMVQ_N1` leaves MMVQ at n=1 as shipped. The kernel default **does** move to the hoisted arm; that is the candidate, and `GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_B_HOIST=0` restores the shipped arm on the same binary. |
+
+### Coverage limits — stated, not hidden
+
+1. **Nothing was compiled.** GLSL syntax, array-parameter passing and the specialization link are
+   reviewed by eye only. Most likely failure mode: a GLSL rule on passing `sc[n]` (a row of a
+   2-D spec-constant-sized array) as an `const FLOAT_TYPE[8]` parameter. If glslang rejects it, the
+   fix is local — pass `dm`/`sc`/`q4` arrays whole plus the index `n`.
+2. **Spill is unmeasured and is the main performance risk.** ~52 VGPRs of decoded weights at
