+## 7. Pairing plan for HQ (run after the chain releases the box)
+
+### Build
+
+```
+cmake --build build --target test-backend-ops -j
+```
+
+Expect two receipt lines on the first Vulkan device init:
+
+```
+ggml_vulkan: q6_k mat-vec direct-scales: ON
+ggml_vulkan: q5_k mat-vec activation-hoist: ON
+```
+
+**One binary serves every arm below.** No second build is needed, and no rebuild between arms —
+that is the point of the spec constant.
+
+### Correctness first (gate; do not measure until this is clean)
+
+```
+build/bin/test-backend-ops test -o MUL_MAT -b Vulkan0
+```
+
+Run it **twice**: once unset, once with `GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_B_HOIST=0`. Both arms must be fully green on
+the new Q5_K rows. The two arms are expected **bit-identical**, so any Q5_K row that is green in one
+and red in the other is a real defect in the hoisted arm — report it and stop.
+
+### Planted red (routing proof — I could not run it, so HQ must)
+
+Two plants are needed because the route splits. Apply **one at a time**, rebuild, observe, then
+`git checkout --` the file to revert.
+
+**Plant 1 — the f32 dequant shader (expect `n = 2..8` red, `n = 1` GREEN under default routing):**
+
+`ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/mul_mat_vec_q5_k.comp:82`
+
+```glsl
+-    const uint32_t qs0_16_lo4_offset16  = ((qh >> (2*v_im)) & 0x01010101) << 4;
++    const uint32_t qs0_16_lo4_offset16  = ((qh >> (2*v_im)) & 0x01010101) << 3;
+```
+
+**Plant 2 — the MMVQ Q5_K arm (expect `n = 1` red, `n = 2..8` GREEN under default routing):**
+
+`ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/mul_mat_vecq_funcs.glsl:389`
+
+```glsl
+-                  (((data_a_packed32[ib_k].qh[qh_idx    ] >> qh_shift) & 0x01010101) << 4),
++                  (((data_a_packed32[ib_k].qh[qh_idx    ] >> qh_shift) & 0x01010101) << 3),
+```
+
+Both drop the Q5_K 5th bit from weight value 16 to 8 on one group — wrong math, no crash, exactly the
+failure a tolerance gate must catch.
+
+**Plant strength (checked by inspection, not run).** `qs0_16_lo4_offset16` is evaluated
+unconditionally by every thread in `decode_superblock()`: `v_im` only selects which bits of `qh` are
+shifted in, it does not guard the statement. So all 16 cooperating threads corrupt 4 of their 16
+weight values — **a quarter of every superblock**, by 8 on a 0..31 scale. That is far above the
+`5e-4` NMSE bound. **Read the plant result on the `m = 7` and `m = 17407` rows first**, however: the
+comment at `test-backend-ops.cpp:10710-10714` records this harness averaging intermittent errors of
+`8.1e-4` against that bound on large `m`, so a wide shape is the weakest place to read a plant. If
+`m = 248320` does not redden, that is the averaging hazard, **not** evidence the route is different —
+the narrow rows are the discriminator. **The complementary pattern is the receipt**: if plant 1 also
+reddens `n = 1`, or plant 2 also reddens `n > 1`, then the routing described in §1 is wrong and every
+number below is mis-attributed. This is the same routing-proof method protected-wins row 58 used for
+S-X8. Plant 1 must also redden both `GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_B_HOIST` arms — if only one goes red, the two
+arms are not sharing `decode_superblock()` the way §2 claims.
+
+### Perf, three interleaved rounds per arm, one quiet hold
+
+Filters (each selects one shape across `n = 1..8`, all three types):
+
+```
+-p "type_a=q5_K,type_b=f32,m=17408"
+-p "type_a=q5_K,type_b=f32,m=5120"
+-p "type_a=q5_K,type_b=f32,m=248320"
+```
+
+Swap `type_a=q4_K` / `type_a=q6_K` for the control rows on the same `m`.
+
+**Arm A — the hoist, at the widths it actually serves (`n = 2..8`).** Default routing.
+
+```
+GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_B_HOIST=0 build/bin/test-backend-ops perf -o MUL_MAT -b Vulkan0 -p "type_a=q5_K,type_b=f32,m=17408"   # base
+                          build/bin/test-backend-ops perf -o MUL_MAT -b Vulkan0 -p "type_a=q5_K,type_b=f32,m=17408"   # candidate
+```
+
+Interleave base/candidate/base/candidate/base/candidate — do not run three of one then three of the
+other. Repeat for the other two filters and for the Q4_K and Q6_K controls.
+
+**Arm B — the open routing question at `n = 1`.** Both sides with `GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_MMVQ_N1=0`, which
+puts `n = 1` on the f32 shader so the hoist is measurable there, and which simultaneously answers
+"does MMVQ still earn `n = 1` for Q5_K?".
+
+```
+GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_MMVQ_N1=0 GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_B_HOIST=0 ... -p "type_a=q5_K,type_b=f32,m=17408"   # base
+GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_MMVQ_N1=0                          ... -p "type_a=q5_K,type_b=f32,m=17408"   # candidate
+```
+
+Also record **MMVQ vs f32 at `n = 1`** directly: default (MMVQ) against `GGML_ARIFI_Q5K_MMVQ_N1=0`
+(f32, hoisted). That single comparison decides whether the `n = 1` default should move, and it is a
+checker's call, not mine.
+
+### Acceptance rule
+
+The briefed rule cannot be applied as written (§1). Proposed replacement, stated so HQ can overrule it:
+
+| # | Arm | Rule |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | A | **Promote the hoist** if median gain `>= +5%` at `n = 4..8` on both FFN shapes (17408x5120 and 5120x17408), **and** no row on any of the three shapes is worse than `-3%` with non-overlapping raw rounds. |
+| 2 | A | **Width step:** per-dispatch cost at `n = 4..8` improves against base by any margin. The absolute "within 1.25x of width 1" target is **reported, not gated** — §2 explains it may be structurally unreachable, and the Q4_K control row is what says so. |
+| 3 | A | **Q4_K control must not move** (within ±3%). If it does, the hold was noisy — discard the round. |
+| 4 | A | **Q6_K must not regress** (protected win `vulkan-q6k-matvec-direct-scales`). It should be flat by construction; a move means the diff leaked. |
+| 5 | B | **Move the `n=1` default to f32 only if** f32+hoist beats MMVQ at `n = 1` by `>= +10%` median on both FFN shapes with non-overlapping rounds. Otherwise leave the shipped route and record the number. |
+
+Rules 1 and 5 are independent: the hoist can promote while the `n=1` route stays on MMVQ.
+
+### Register/occupancy receipt (cheap, and it is the one that explains a loss)
+
+If arm A loses, the spill hypothesis in §6.2 is the first suspect. Capture it rather than guessing:
+
+```
+RADV_DEBUG=shaderstats build/bin/test-backend-ops perf -o MUL_MAT -b Vulkan0 -p "type_a=q5_K,type_b=f32,m=17408"
+```
